GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 57(b)(1) — the income for a separate computation, the conditions being` `the main work of both spouses who are members is qualifying work` `and` `the work of each spouse is needed to produce the kibbutz's income` `and` `the kibbutz kept exact records of the work of all its members, in the kibbutz and outside it` `with taxable income` `the kibbutz's taxable income as computed for paragraph (a)` `less` `the taxable income that is not income under section 2(1) or 2(2)` MEANS
    IF   `the main work of both spouses who are members is qualifying work` AND `the work of each spouse is needed to produce the kibbutz's income` AND `the kibbutz kept exact records of the work of all its members, in the kibbutz and outside it`
    THEN `the kibbutz's taxable income as computed for paragraph (a)` MINUS `the taxable income that is not income under section 2(1) or 2(2)`
    ELSE `section 57(b)(1) lets the kibbutz claim a separate computation only if its three conditions hold`
